RustCGoPythonNode.js <p><code>indicator()</code> returns a <code>Result</code>. The <code>IndicatorError</code> enum covers the common failure cases:</p> Variant Cause <code>IndicatorError::NotEnoughData</code> Input length is shorter than the indicator's minimum lookback <code>IndicatorError::InvalidOption</code> An option value is out of range (e.g. period &lt; 1) <code>IndicatorError::InputLengthMismatch</code> Multi-input indicators received slices of different lengths <pre><code>match [indicator].indicator(&amp;[close.as_slice()], &amp;[5.0], None) {
    Ok((outputs, state)) =&gt; { /* use outputs */ }
    Err(e) =&gt; eprintln!("Indicator error: {e}"),
}
</code></pre> <p>Every <code>CIndicatorResult</code> starts with an <code>error</code> field of type <code>CIndicatorError</code>. Check it against <code>C_INDICATOR_ERROR_OK</code>:</p> <pre><code>CIndicatorResult r = &lt;ind&gt;_indicator(inputs, len, options, NULL, 0);
if (r.error != C_INDICATOR_ERROR_OK) {
    fprintf(stderr, "&lt;ind&gt; failed: error=%d\n", r.error);
    return 1;
}
